+			/* Start the timer.
+			 *
+			 * RNSBox: moved this inside
+			 * the new-NDP block. Original upstream code restarts
+			 * the hrtimer on EVERY datagram. Under sustained load
+			 * (>3-4k pkt/s),
+			 * each packet kept pushing the timer forward, so the
+			 * NTB only flushed when it hit dwNtbInMaxSize (16KB).
+			 * That stalled small flows (interactive TCP, ACKs) for
+			 * milliseconds and starved the host side of usable NCM
+			 * NTBs, hard-capping tunnel throughput at ~25 Mbps on
+			 * a 1 GHz core. Bounding the NTB age at TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS
+			 * after the FIRST datagram of an NDP fixes both.
